      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 11:01 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2003-02-9065",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d2d6a8984ae199b88e25907861c991fa88c1ca9672ddd0328a86cb68fc20a247",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d2d6a8984ae1-0000-0001",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The petitioner in this case, Shakur Muhammad, is a state prisoner who has brought a civil rights action alleging that a prison guard framed him on a false disciplinary charge in retaliation for his having exercised his constitutional right to seek redress in the courts for this same prison guard's previous misconduct."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Unnamed Justice",
      "case_id": "2003-02-9065",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d2d6a8984ae199b88e25907861c991fa88c1ca9672ddd0328a86cb68fc20a247",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d2d6a8984ae1-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: But I don't understand this about this case. I'm having an awfully hard time understanding this case, and - and it seemed to me what had happened was that the - your client, who's certainly well represented, he is sitting there at lunch and he makes some faces or gestures and the prison guard then has him up for a couple of charges and he basically is acquitted of the more serious one and they punish him for the more - less serious, threatening behavior, no, it's insolence or something like that."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2003-02-9065",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d2d6a8984ae199b88e25907861c991fa88c1ca9672ddd0328a86cb68fc20a247",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d2d6a8984ae1-0000-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. BECKWITH: Well, that's right, and you know, this is undoubtedly a valid First Amendment retaliation claim."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Beckwith",
      "case_id": "2003-02-9065",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d2d6a8984ae199b88e25907861c991fa88c1ca9672ddd0328a86cb68fc20a247",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d2d6a8984ae1-0001-0001",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "That's correct, Justice Scalia, and if good-time credits are not at issue, it doesn't matter if we're challenging the insolence conviction, because nothing about this claim is going to affect the fact or duration of - of confinement, so that, you know -"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2003-02-9065",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d2d6a8984ae199b88e25907861c991fa88c1ca9672ddd0328a86cb68fc20a247",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d2d6a8984ae1-0001-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Mr. Muhammad exhausted, without seeking rehearing he exhausted."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent",
      "case_id": "2003-02-9065",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d2d6a8984ae199b88e25907861c991fa88c1ca9672ddd0328a86cb68fc20a247",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d2d6a8984ae1-0001-0006",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The damages are this, you know, the chilling effect, the six days of pre-hearing detention, but that's just a remedial question."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent",
      "case_id": "2003-02-9065",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d2d6a8984ae199b88e25907861c991fa88c1ca9672ddd0328a86cb68fc20a247",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d2d6a8984ae1-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I agree this is a very confusing case. We believe there are several reasons why summary judgment should be affirmed."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2003-02-9065",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "d2d6a8984ae199b88e25907861c991fa88c1ca9672ddd0328a86cb68fc20a247",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d2d6a8984ae1-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: You could have made a motion to remand or something."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2003-02-9065",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "d2d6a8984ae199b88e25907861c991fa88c1ca9672ddd0328a86cb68fc20a247",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d2d6a8984ae1-0002-0002",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The petitioner filed a motion for rehearing."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Casey",
      "case_id": "2003-02-9065",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "d2d6a8984ae199b88e25907861c991fa88c1ca9672ddd0328a86cb68fc20a247",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d2d6a8984ae1-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Because as in the Edwards v. Balisok and - and Heck v. Humphrey, the proper method of analysis is to look to the most closely analogous common law tort, look to traditions of common law, public policy considerations in light of the purposes of Section 1983."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2003-02-9065",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "d2d6a8984ae199b88e25907861c991fa88c1ca9672ddd0328a86cb68fc20a247",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d2d6a8984ae1-0002-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: I don't see the difference in the Sixth Circuit rule anymore. What - in what respect is it in the minority?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Beckwith",
      "case_id": "2003-02-9065",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "d2d6a8984ae199b88e25907861c991fa88c1ca9672ddd0328a86cb68fc20a247",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d2d6a8984ae1-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 51,
        "start": 51
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Turning to the actual question presented in this case, there is no justification for the Sixth Circuit's rule extending the Heck favorable termination requirement to prison hearings that don't involve the fact or duration of custody."
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
